/-!
# The first rebuild's bytes, parsed

The first rebuild (suffix 1426–2714) hashes a transaction it assembles from the pieces and the spend's own
fields, and compares the hash with the grandparent's txid (`rebuildA_fact1`). Under second-preimage freedom
those bytes are the grandparent's serialisation, so the grandparent is what `decodeTx` reads from them. This
file names the bytes (`rebuiltA`), lays them out field by field for each of the two optional arms (`rebuiltA_00`
… `rebuiltA_11`: a second token input when the piece at depth 182 is non-zero, as a merge commit has, and a second
proof output when the piece at depth 140 is non-zero, as a split commit has) and reads them (`decode_rebuiltA`):
the first input spends the settled token with the unlocking script the rebuild assembles (`scA0`), the optional
second token input has its own (`scA2`), the last input is the fee input; the outputs are the commit token
(`lkA`, the pieces at depths 142–151 with the spend's issuer push and suffix), the pay-to-proof output, the
optional second one, and a P2PKH output. The decode takes the widths the parse reads as hypotheses (`WidthsA`):
the run fixes some of them (the version, the scripts' varints), the rest are pieces the bytes push without a
size check. Generated by the glue's `gen_rebuilt.py` from the region's facts; regenerate rather than edit.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSimpArgs false
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option maxRecDepth 100000
set_option linter.unusedVariables false

namespace BoltProof.Glue.SimpleMulti

